# At a Russian wedding: the man standing by the window
subtitle: "Мужчи́ну, стоя́щего у окна́; о де́вушке, сидя́щей ря́дом: Russian participles change case like adjectives, at Иван and Лена's wedding."
tags: ["russian","russian participles","participles in cases","russian wedding","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/participles","vocabulary/family"]
thumb: "band \"Who's the man by the window?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"It's getting dark in Russian: темнеет, мне повезло","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/194-russian-impersonal.cast"}

